  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>mcp_call_tools - calls the lookup_order tool of the Ridgeline Outfitters MCP server once per order id, with
no LLM, and writes each order's status.
Needs the MCP connection retail-tools in your metastore.

1. csvi-orders: CSV file input, ../order_ids.csv, one field order_id (String).
2. mcp-lookup-order: MCP Client, connection retail-tools, Call tool, Native tool lookup_order, Native
   arguments {"order_id": "{{order_id}}"}; result tool_result, error tool_error, timeout 30.
3. frow-tool-ok: Filter rows, tool_error IS NULL; true to json-order, false to txt-order-errors.
4. json-order: JSON input from the field tool_result: customer_first_name, status, carrier, tracking_number,
   estimated_delivery, delivered_on, item_count (Integer), status_note.
5. sv-order: Select values, keeps order_id and the eight order fields, in that order.
6. txt-order-status: Text file output, ${Internal.Entry.Current.Directory}/order_status.csv.
7. txt-order-errors: Text file output, ${Internal.Entry.Current.Directory}/order_errors.csv: the rows whose
   tool call failed.

Shipped data: 6 order ids; A1001 to A1005 exist on the server, A9999 does not and goes to
order_errors.csv.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>625</width>
      <heigth>314</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
